[58:31] orchestrator     directive 2 from steer: code/lean/Lib/Statement.lean compiles but does not state H16.2, and lean_check did not catch either defect. Fix both before any further Lean work. FIRST: PlanarPolyField.degree_at_most is the literal placeholder 'True', so h16_2 quantifies over every map Plane to Plane rather than over polynomial fields. Replace it with the real hypothesis - each coordinate function is in MvPolynomial (Fin 2) real with totalDegree at most n, evaluated via MvPolynomial.eval - so the binder carries the degree bound. As written the statement is not H16.2 and is false, since a smooth field can be a counterexample to it. SECOND: limitCycleCount uses Set.ncard, which is 0 for an infinite set, so a field with infinitely many limit cycles satisfies the bound trivially and the finiteness assertion - the whole content of the problem - is quantified away. State it as (LimitCycleSet f.X).Finite together with the cardinality bound, or as a Set.Finite plus ncard conjunction. Then re-run lean_check and report the verdict. Record both defects as a finding: a Lean file that compiles is not a Lean file that means the mathematics, and neither the tautology check nor the retired-binder check caught a True placeholder or an ncard-on-infinite-set hole.
